        <p>Every setting <code>atlas config</code> manages in 0.1.55, 122 in all, grouped by area. Under each setting is its type and whether a running daemon picks up a change without a restart: <code>live</code> means the knob is re-read per call or tick, <code>restart</code> means restart to apply it. A value is written in the syntax its environment variable accepts, in the environment, in <code>.atlas/settings.json</code> or with <code>atlas config set</code>. The settings new in 0.1.55 are listed in the <a className="text-link" href="#docs/upgrade">release notes</a>.</p>
